course: dictionary
lesson: 3605
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word fig is a good example. «Look at Fig. 3 in your science book» means look at picture number 3, because Fig. is short for figure. «Dried figs are a healthy snack» means the sweet fruit.
explain: Read the words around the word first. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. Does «Look at picture number 3» fit? Yes, so Fig. here is short for figure.
explain: Old-fashioned phrases can be tricky too. «I don't give a fig» does not mean you give away a fruit. It means you do not care at all, because a fig is something worth nothing. Context and a dictionary together settle it.
fact: A fig is a soft, sweet fruit with many tiny seeds inside, shaped like a small pear.
fact: The fig tree is the tree that this fruit grows on.
fact: «Fig.» is short for «figure», a numbered picture or diagram in a book.
fact: In the Bible, Adam and Eve made clothes from fig leaves.
fact: «I don't give a fig» is an old-fashioned phrase meaning you do not care at all.
exercise: «Dried figs are a healthy snack.» What is a fig here? | Something worth a lot of money | *A sweet fruit with tiny seeds inside | A numbered picture in a book | A tree with no leaves
exercise: «Look at Fig. 2 on page six.» What does Fig. mean? | Fast | Finish | *Figure, a numbered picture or diagram | Fig tree
exercise: «I don't give a fig about the score.» What does fig mean here? | A green leaf | A picture in a book | *Something worth nothing, so I do not care | A sweet fruit
test: «Zacchaeus climbed a sycamore-fig tree to see Jesus.» Which meaning of fig is used? | A small pear-shaped bird | Something worth nothing | *The tree that figs grow on | A numbered picture
test: «A strangler fig starts from a seed dropped high on a tree by a bird.» What does fig mean here? | A picture in a science book | Something worth nothing | *A kind of fig tree, the plant itself | A fruit you can dry
exam: Which sentence uses fig to mean a numbered picture? | Dried figs are sweet and chewy | *See Fig. 4 for the labelled diagram | The fig tree grew by the river | I don't give a fig what they think
